-- title:
--   Second inequality for a prime Kummer layer
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $E$ be number fields with $E$ a $k$-algebra, and let $p$ be a prime. Assume $k$ contains a primitive $p$-th root of unity (the set `primitiveRoots p k` is nonempty), that $[E:k]=p$, and that $E/k$ is Galois. Assume furthermore the first-inequality input over $E$ at $p$: for every number field $M$ that is a Galois $E$-algebra with $[M:E]=p$ and every ideal $\mathfrak{f}_0$ of $\mathcal{O}_E$ that is admissible at $p$ for $M/E$, i.e. $\mathfrak{f}_0\neq 0$ and $v^{2e+1}\mid\mathfrak{f}_0$ for every prime $v$ of $E$ such that the chosen prime of $M$ above $v$ has nontrivial inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(M/E)$, where $e$ is the ramification index of the ideal $(p)$ at $v$, the predicate `IdeleFirstIneqDataAt E M 𝔣₀` holds: there is a homomorphism $\mathrm{Nrm}$ from the idele units of $M$ to those of $E$ which carries adjusters at level $\mathfrak{f}_0\mathcal{O}_M$ to adjusters at level $\mathfrak{f}_0$ (the field element being replaced by its norm), whose composition with the finite ideal-content map agrees with the relative norm of ideal units applied to the content, whose image contains the unit ideles of level $\mathfrak{f}_0$ whenever $\mathfrak{f}_0$ is an admissible modulus for $M/E$, and with $[M:E]$ dividing the index of the subgroup generated by the principal ideles and the image of $\mathrm{Nrm}$. Then for every ideal $\mathfrak{f}$ of $\mathcal{O}_k$ the conclusion `SecondInequalityCTM k E 𝔣` holds: inside the group of ideal units coprime to $\mathfrak{f}$, the index of the subgroup generated by the narrow ray subgroup modulo $\mathfrak{f}$ and the image of the relative norm map `relNormCTM k E 𝔣` divides $\#\mathrm{Gal}(E/k)$.
--
--   This is the second inequality of class field theory (Takagi's algebraic inequality) in its Kummer-theoretic form for a cyclic layer of prime degree $p$ over a base containing the $p$-th roots of unity, with the dependence on the first inequality over the upper field recorded as an explicit hypothesis. It is the inductive step used by [`NumberField.PrimeNormIndex.secondInequalityCTM_of_finrank_eq_prime`](thm.html#NumberField.PrimeNormIndex.secondInequalityCTM_of_finrank_eq_prime) and [`NumberField.PrimeNormIndex.secondInequalityCTM_of_finrank_eq_three`](thm.html#NumberField.PrimeNormIndex.secondInequalityCTM_of_finrank_eq_three).
